{"tool_name":"caftools","contents":["oeb","debian","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"caftools","home":"http://www.sanger.ac.uk/science/tools/caf","summary":"CAFTOOLS comprises a set of libraries and programs for manipulating DNA sequence assemblies using CAF files, a comprehensive representation of a sequence assembly as a text file.","addition_date":"2017-12-18T00:04:32Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-11T14:55:04Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["2.0.2"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:caftools","credit":[{"name":"Richard Durbin","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9130-1006","typeEntity":"Person"},{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.sanger.ac.uk/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.sanger.ac.uk/science/tools/caf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"CAFTOOLS","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"Large-scale genomic sequencing requires a software infrastructure to support and integrate applications that are not directly compatible. We describe a suite of software tools built around the Common Assembly Format (CAF), a comprehensive representation of a sequence assembly as a text file. These tools form the backbone of sequencing informatics at the Sanger Centre and the Genome Sequencing Center. The CAF format is intentionally flexible, and our Perl and C libraries, which parse and manipulate it, provide powerful tools for creating new applications as well as wrappers to incorporate other software. The tools are available free by anonymous FTP from ftp://ftp.sanger.ac.uk/pub/badger/.","authors":[{"name":"Dear S."},{"name":"Durbin R."},{"name":"Hillier L."},{"name":"Marth G."},{"name":"Mott R."},{"name":"Thierry-Mieg J."}],"citatio